ph native Linux package

Configuration: /etc/ph; state: /var/lib/ph. Services run as root.
Add subscriptions with sudo ph subscription add, then seed with sudo ph update.
ph refresh requests the native update service; no sudo policy is installed.
ph update updates subscriptions, not software. Use the package manager to upgrade.

Mixed proxy: 127.0.0.1:1080; core API: 127.0.0.1:9090. No TUN or host routing.
The unauthenticated core API trusts all local users and exposes runtime
configuration controls. Do not use these defaults with untrusted local users
or give root-run services user-writable configuration, templates, or state.

Upgrades preserve state and edited configuration. Removal retains private state;
Debian purge removes native conffiles. Delete provider secrets manually.
Installation and service commands: https://github.com/sleroq/proxy-helper/blob/master/docs/linux.md

Bundled sing-box and mihomo are GPLv3 projects. License texts are supplied as
LICENSE-sing-box and LICENSE-mihomo. Sources:
